# API Route Conventions

- Keep route handlers thin: validate -> service call -> respond.
- Always wrap service calls in try/catch using `handleServiceError` from `src/lib/api-errors.ts`.
- Return consistent error shapes: `{ error: string }` with appropriate HTTP status.
- Every model with a collection route should have a corresponding `[id]` route with at least GET and PATCH.

# Error Handling

- P2002 (unique constraint) → 409 Conflict with human-readable field name.
- P2025 (record not found) → 404 Not Found.
- Unknown errors → 500 Internal Server Error (logged to console).
- Client pages must display errors via `sonner` toast, never swallow them silently.

# Audit

- All config mutations (create, update, deactivate) must emit an audit event after success.
- Use `createAuditEvent()` from `src/modules/audit/service.ts` with `.catch(() => {})` for non-blocking writes.
